{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550022-any-light-machine-guns-in-the-original-werewolf","id":1550022,"title":"Any Light Machine Guns in the original Werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-10T19:37:26-07:00","id":1550022,"title":"Any Light Machine Guns in the original Werewolf?","content":"Saw a topic like this on another site, thought I'd ask here; are there any mentions of Light Machine Gun weapons in the original Werewolf: the Apocalypse game line? There's a number of other gun types mentioned, like pistols, revolvers, assault rifles, shotguns, SMGs, sniper rifles, rocket launchers, and even team/vehicle-mounted Heavy Machine Guns in Rage Across the Amazon, but there's a distinct lack of LMGs, like the M60 or the M249.<br /> <br /> I know there's stats for an M60 in the Combat manual for the World of Darkness in general, but anything for Werewolf in particular? They wouldn't be used all that much, but there should be something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T00:05:15-07:00","id":1550025,"title":"","content":"M20 has a .30 machine gun. The Vampire 2nd edition player's guide also had an extensive list of weapons, military ones and machine guns included (though the system broke down after reaching aircraft machine guns. Tank cannon damage became astronomical and capable of gibbing 4th gens).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T01:28:52-07:00","id":1550027,"title":"","content":"I don't believe WtA specifically has ever covered LMGs.<br /> <br /> That said... most LMGs use the same or largely similar ammunition to assault rifles, with the primary difference being capacity; though what's considered effective ranges for LMGs is usually significantly farther than for semi-automatic or bolt action rifles because of intended use.<br /> <br /> While I can understand the desire for it... I'm not really sure it's all the important to the game. The WoD games aren't very good war simulators, and the heavy weapons and combat vehicle rules are rarely something people talk about using frequently if at all. Large scale combat tends to take focus off the PCs, which generally isn't fun for the players unless the group really likes to get into that style of play (and speaking as someone that does like that sort of stuff... trying to bend and twist the WoD rules to function with it is... unsatisfying).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T13:55:43-07:00","id":1550057,"title":"","content":"Can't disagree that they don't fit the feel of the game, it's urban fantasy, and LMGs don't fit that very well. Just found it weird that they were basically the only type of weapon that didn't get referenced in Werewolf; you'd think a First Team or something would pack one for dealing with a Garou pack, but there's nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T14:59:16-07:00","id":1550062,"title":"","content":"M20 has a lot of firearms stats as Saur Ops Specialist said:<br /> <br /> The .30 caliber machine gun deal 12 dice damage, has 100 rounds in magazine, a firing rate of 5<br /> The .50 caliber machine gun deal 16 dice damage, has 200 rounds in magazine, a firing rate of 5, can only be used when mounted on a vehicle<br /> <br /> That said, this kind of weapons should not be used by the st unless in a critical war type mission, it'be absurd to see a pentex patrol with one of those in the forest. The only kind of machine gun these threat could have in a regular fight would be something like m240 or m60, with the same damage as an assault rifle; 7 dice damage as Heavy Arms said. The only benefit they'd get is the huge amount of round in a single magazine<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> After some research it appear that the .30 caliber use 7.62mm round, wich is the same caliber for m60 and the one depicted in M20. The descriptions i've found tell that Light Machine Guns such as m240 and m60 have more firepower than assault rifle while being weaker than big machine guns like those mounted on tripod. One of the reason is the longer canon that allows the round to gain more speed before getting out of the rifle, so with the same caliber firepower is like Assault Rifle &lt; Light Machine Guns &lt; Machines guns (AK-47 is an assault rifle and also use 7.62 rounds)<br /> <br /> I you feel like it, give the same damage pool as the shotgun to the LMG, and keep the .30 machine gun as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 04-12-2025, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T15:58:46-07:00","id":1550064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550022-any-light-machine-guns-in-the-original-werewolf?p=1550057#post1550057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't disagree that they don't fit the feel of the game, it's urban fantasy, and LMGs don't fit that very well. Just found it weird that they were basically the only type of weapon that didn't get referenced in Werewolf; you'd think a First Team or something would pack one for dealing with a Garou pack, but there's nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guerilla war is still war. You won't find them frequently but you're more likely to find them in W:tA than in other WoD games because open war is on the table, even if not likely to happen within US borders or the like.<br /> <br /> But Garou have often flocked to open war zones in the past for one reason or another. So, again, if you were going to see it anywhere, it's either here, or a Technocracy game by someone who really likes their MilSF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T22:59:19-07:00","id":1550140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550022-any-light-machine-guns-in-the-original-werewolf?p=1550062#post1550062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One of the reason is the longer canon that allows the round to gain more speed before getting out of the rifle, so with the same caliber firepower is like Assault Rifle &lt; Light Machine Guns &lt; Machines guns (AK-47 is an assault rifle and also use 7.62 rounds)</div> </div> </div> </div>But the 7.62 ammunition used in an AK-47 (7.62x39) is not the same (and far less powerfull) as the one used in an m60 (7.62x52).<br /> <br /> There are Assault Rifle (nowadays typically called Battle Rifles) that use 7.62x52 (like the M14, the AR10, the G3 and the FAL), while there are also Machines guns that use the less powerfull rounds of the current Assault Rifles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T11:48:09-07:00","id":1550162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550022-any-light-machine-guns-in-the-original-werewolf?p=1550062#post1550062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, this kind of weapons should not be used by the st unless in a critical war type mission, it'be absurd to see a pentex patrol with one of those in the forest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to disagree.<br /> <br /> On top of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> said on Garou in war zones, I have to add that military equipment can be and is frequently found in the hands of criminals. Add to this that while real world corporations don't get their hands on those things, it is a trope well within the genre for WtA. Pentex is both a corporation, fraught with illegal operations, and EVIL. And their operations see frequent intervention from Werewolves and other Bio-Spiritual Weapons of Mass Destruction.<br /> <br /> All things considered, while they shouldn't be common, LMG and HMG should definitely be on the table for any WtA chronicle at some point, and for some of them should be there frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:03:33-07:00","id":1550163,"title":"","content":"Also, Pentex has an arms manufacturer or two under its umbrella, and it's likely far from the only WIC to do so. This clip from Robocop applies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KPMdnicSen8\" data-code=\"KPMdnicSen8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KPMdnicSen8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}